text:
Lifelong resident of this fine suburb:
PROS:
- about as diverse in terms of languages/races as one can get regionally;
- welcoming of the vast majority of people, so long as those people are not "antisocial";
- very close to, arguably, *the greatest city on the planet*, NYC, and all its excitement;
- much safer than the media would have one believe, despite the more average income level locally, overall, along with proximity to economically disadvantaged places like Paterson;
- centrally located to many other parts of the immediate area (downtowns/malls/etc.)...
CONS:
- council/various local boards tend to be "secretive";
- could use some better cleaning/pickup services most days;
- somehow manages to be hostile to *both cars and public transportation*;
- overdevelopment has unfortunately crept into this suburb, the way it has crept into other local suburbs;
- proximity to disadvantaged places like Paterson means the occasional bit of violence *does occur locally*...
